# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps secrets out of it.
#
# Without this, `docker build .` uploads the whole working tree as build context
# - including target/ (a ~365 MB fat jar) and .env. Even though the Dockerfile
# never COPYs .env today, anything that later does `COPY . .` would bake your
# OpenRouter key into an image layer permanently.

# build output - the jar is built inside the image by the multi-stage build,
# so the host's target/ is never needed as context
target/

# secrets - never send these to the daemon
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p12
*.jks

# local caches
.cache/

# vcs and tooling
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea/
.vscode/
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# docs, diagrams and logs are not needed to build the jar
*.log
*.md
!HELP.md
src/main/resources/docs/
